cff-version: 1.2.0
title: >-
  Upstream processing pipeline (FASTQ to gene counts) for the
  Pax6 mouse cornea and trigeminal ganglion RNA-seq
message: >-
  If you use this software, please cite it and the paper whose
  analysis you are reproducing.
type: software
authors:
  - given-names: James D.
    family-names: Lauderdale
    affiliation: >-
      Department of Cellular Biology, University of Georgia,
      Athens, GA 30602, USA
    email: jdlauder@uga.edu
    orcid: 'https://orcid.org/0000-0001-7503-0528'
  - given-names: Sneha K.
    family-names: Mohan
    affiliation: >-
      Department of Cellular Biology, University of Georgia,
      Athens, GA 30602, USA
repository-code: 'https://github.com/Lauderdale-Lab/pax6-cornea-trigeminal-rnaseq-upstream'
abstract: >-
  Manifest-driven SLURM pipeline for read QC and trimming
  (Trimmomatic), alignment (HISAT2, GRCm38), measured
  strandedness, and fragment-level gene counting (featureCounts,
  GENCODE vM25), producing the count matrices analysed in
  pax6-cornea-nerve-vascular-transparency,
  pax6-adult-cornea-transcriptome and
  pax6-cornea-development-transcriptome.
keywords:
  - RNA-seq
  - HISAT2
  - featureCounts
  - cornea
  - Pax6
license: MIT
version: 1.0.0
